{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/55937-why-does-cult-cost-so-much","id":55937,"title":"Why Does Cult Cost So Much?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-22T21:32:51-08:00","id":55937,"title":"Why Does Cult Cost So Much?","content":"Why does a dot of Reach or Grasp cost the equivalent of a 2 dot merit? It seems very strange and overly expensive to me, and it has been bothering me for some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T22:31:23-08:00","id":55962,"title":"","content":"To get a good cult with Reach or Grasp at about 3 and 2 requires 20 XP after character generation. It's a bit expensive to start off with a good cult, but it's basically the same as being really proficient in martial arts, it's going to cost you a lot. Plus cults get a +1 to Reach and Grasp when working near the tomb so there's that. I'll agree it's expensive to start out with a good cult but that's kind of par for the course for everything in WoD. Thematically you're really strong in mummy but just like every other person or being in WoD you're broke and need to work your way up. It's part of the game. Really though it's not that hard to just say it costs 1 dot or half a dot, but probably the best thing to do is just keep the prices as they are during character generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T22:45:19-08:00","id":55969,"title":"","content":"Eh. I'm mostly just asking because I wanted to get a sense for the logic behind it. I already house ruled it so that Reach and Grasp are 1 dot merits for anything I do.<br /> <br /> But then, I also run with GMC too and Mummy isn't built for that either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T03:43:44-08:00","id":56033,"title":"","content":"I think that each dot of Reach or Grasp costing the equivalent of a 2-dot Merit is a roundabout way of introducing flat XP costs for Cults. Buying 5 dots in Reach would still cost the same as 5 dots in a normal Merit (30 XP).<br /> <br /> I agree with making it 1-dot Merits under GMC, as that way it stays equivalent to normal Merits in costs. Otherwise Cults would become far more expensive than normal Merits, where they weren't earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T04:22:01-08:00","id":56042,"title":"","content":"because in addition to letting you mess with the cults of other mummy's (as a dice pool penalty and bearing in mind that the dice pool is normally going to be no more then six) and giving you battle fodder (the longer you give the cult to get ready the better the fodder) they give you access to Allies, Contacts and Resources (granted at one dot less then the rating but still) social merits don't react well to the passing of century's. lets say that a mummy (for our purposes we will call him Mr White) has a tribal cult, he has sunk a far few of his char-gen merit dots into Reach since he wants to be above board, we'll say he spent 4 dots, so his reach is three (four near his tomb) his grasp on the other hand is only one (two near his tomb). <br /> <br /> Mr white wants to spend a night wining and dining a socialite who owns a relic Mr White wants to acquire, one catch, he has no scratch, and no way to get into the restaurant he wants. So he calls on his cult, first he needs an ally who can get him a reservation with the restaurant, lets say that a two dot ally will do the trick, because his cult is a tribe he has no issue with finding an ally within the cult who either works at the restaurant or has enough pull to get him a reservation.<br /> <br /> Now he needs cash (he has to pay for the meal somehow) and to get the cash he needs to do a &quot;visible magical miracle&quot; to get the cult to shower him in gold/give him diamonds/do funds transfers into his bank account, three dots of resources will be more then enough for the bill. he only has reach three though which would mean that he can only get two dots of resources. unless he is near his tomb, more cultists means more witness's means more resources. He decides to use second tier of the utterance Awaken the Dead to call a Corpse Thrall within his cults main ritual chamber about 500 meters from his tomb, Visible? check. Magical? check. Miracle? check. near his tomb? check. of course now he has an Lifeless monstrosity that wants to eat his cultists to deal with...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2080-protector152","name":"Protector152","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:17:14-07:00","id":249375,"title":"","content":"Apologies for bumping something from the last Sothic turn but this is still confusing me and I can't seem to find a completely clear clarification on it.<br /> <br /> Say, for example, I've got a Tribal Cult, with Reach 3 and Grasp 1, by end of character creation. I decide to buy a dot each in Reach and Grasp. Do I:<br /> <br /> 1) Put four more dots in my existing four dot Cult Merit. Total cost: 10+12+14+16=52xp<br /> 2) Put two more dots in my existing four dot Reach merit, and buy a new two dot Grasp merit. Total cost: 10+12+2+4=28xp<br /> 3) Buy a new two dot Reach merit (of which I already have two), and a new two dot Grasp merit. Total cost: 2+4+2+4=12xp<br /> <br /> From what I've gathered from reading through this and a couple of other threads option 3 seems to be the one people are using, but I'd like a clear yes or no on it if possible, because by the rulebook it could honestly be any of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3808-n0z3k1ll3r","name":"n0z3k1ll3r","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T14:05:57-07:00","id":254606,"title":"","content":"It's a flat cost. Each dot is a new two-dot Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}